  <activityDataset>
    <activityDescription>
      <activity id="12e51035-c2a4-57c6-bb23-abb045a23399" activityNameId="f5dce3dd-805d-5cad-8969-b2ec0c695a57" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Transport, passenger, helicopter, single-engine, Betrieb</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Transport, passenger, helicopter, single-engine, Betrieb
A single engine helicopter of the type ecureuil-as-350-b3  with a weight of 1200kg and a life time of 10000 flight hours is assumed. The average flight duration is assumed to be 20min and 3 LTO per hour is required. Specific cruise emission factors for a ecureuil-as-350-b3 helicopter is provided of the federal office of civil aviation (FOCCA);
UUID: 73d97e5c-726d-3fe6-8dad-6201354e15b7
This dataset describes the demand of helicopter, demand of LTOs, energy requirements and emissions of one hour helicopter flight.
Location: &lt;null&gt;
Technology: Data is for an average Swiss helicopter for observation flights (1280kg) using kerosene
Time period: Time of publications
Production volume: hh
Sampling: Statistics 
Extrapolations: helicopter input is extrapolated by a medium haul aircraft.
Uncertainty adjustments: None
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_73d97e5c-726d-3fe6-8dad-6201354e15b7.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
      <geography geographyId="fdab769f-4bdb-5024-8349-c1745bbb2597" geographyContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83">
